<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Seisyllwg</h1><p class="st-meta">730 CE – 920 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Welsh kingdom of Ceredigion and Ystrad Tywi, named after King Seisyll, which merged with Dyfed to form Deheubarth.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Seisyllwg was created when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seisyll-ap-clydog">Seisyll ap Clydog</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ceredigion">Ceredigion</a> added <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ystrad-tywi">Ystrad Tywi</a>, the Tywi valley, to his realm in the 8th century. The new territory was named after him. Little else is known of its early rulers beyond genealogies.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom covered much of later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cardiganshire">Cardiganshire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carmarthenshire">Carmarthenshire</a>, a land of upland pasture and coastal farms with important churches such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/llanbadarn-fawr">Llanbadarn Fawr</a>. Its last native king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gwgon-ap-meurig">Gwgon</a>, drowned in 871, and it passed by marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhodri-the-great">Rhodri the Great</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-gwynedd">Gwynedd</a>, whose son Cadell inherited it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Cadell's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hywel-dda">Hywel Dda</a> united Seisyllwg with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dyfed">Dyfed</a> around 920, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-deheubarth">Kingdom of Deheubarth</a>. The name Seisyllwg fell out of use, though <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ceredigion">Ceredigion</a> persists as a county.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-seisyllwg.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Seisyllwg" width="320" height="453"><figcaption>Image: AlexD · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wales_900-950_(Hywel_the_Good).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>730 CE – 920 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Seisyll ap Clydog, Gwgon, Cadell ap Rhodri</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Welsh</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Seisyllwg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=825&amp;focus=kingdom-of-seisyllwg" aria-label="Kingdom of Seisyllwg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4590 346 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Seisyllwg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4910 602L4910 602M4910 602L4912 613M4910 602L4909 640M4910 602L4904 640"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4910 602h0M4912 613h0M4909 640h0M4904 640h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4910 602h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4910 602h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=825&amp;focus=kingdom-of-seisyllwg">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
